    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0911" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795A.5/10–650: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Anderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-10-06T17:00:00+01:00">October 6, 1950—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 6—1:36 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>357. Depcirtel 9, October 5. We have no information which would throw light on
                    intentions Chinese Communists or Soviet Union re Korea.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office not yet in code telegraph communication with Denmark Minister
                    Peking and latter’s despatches show restraint owing to lack of safe courier
                    service.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Anderson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
